<title>BULGARIA: YIELDS FALL ON BULGARIA 1-, 4-WEEK DISCOUNT T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS FALL ON BULGARIA 1-, 4-WEEK DISCOUNT T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell at Tuesday's</p>
<p>auctions of Bulgaria's Finance Ministry one-week and four-week</p>
<p>discount T-bills, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yields to maturity of the two issues were 1.69</p>
<p>percent and 10.69 percent, respectively, down from 1.95 and</p>
<p>12.75 percent at Monday's auctions.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 81.688 billion levs of</p>
<p>T-bills for today's auctions but the ministry approved bids for</p>
<p>53.035 billion levs worth of paper.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3028097007	 BG3028197005</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     25,000 mln levs    40,000 mln levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    April 15	     April 15</p>
<p> Maturity date		 April 22	     May 13</p>
<p> Bids received		 13,035 mln levs    68,652.8 mln</p>
<p> levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   98.34 pct	    90.09</p>
<p> Bids approved		 13,035 mln levs    40,000 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  98.34 pct	    90.34 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     1.69 pct	     10.69 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
